{
 "segments": [
  {
   "id": "hero-01",
   "scene": "hero",
   "lang": "en",
   "text": "Naṣb. When does a word end in fatha?",
   "pause": 0.6,
   "cues": [
    "title"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "hero-02",
   "scene": "hero",
   "lang": "en",
   "text": "Some words in a verb sentence answer a question about the action.",
   "pause": 0.3,
   "cues": [
    "sub"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "hero-03",
   "scene": "hero",
   "lang": "en",
   "text": "What? Why? When? Where? How?",
   "pause": 0.6,
   "cues": []
  },
  {
   "id": "hero-04",
   "scene": "hero",
   "lang": "en",
   "text": "Those words take naṣb.",
   "pause": 0.6,
   "cues": []
  },
  {
   "id": "c01-title-01",
   "scene": "c01-title",
   "lang": "en",
   "text": "Chapter one. Where we are.",
   "pause": 0.4,
   "cues": [
    "title"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "c01-title-02",
   "scene": "c01-title",
   "lang": "en",
   "text": "There are four cases. We know two. Today we add the third.",
   "pause": 0.5,
   "cues": [
    "sub"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "c01-cases-01",
   "scene": "c01-cases",
   "lang": "en",
   "text": "Case A is rafʿ, with damma. We have learned it.",
   "pause": 0.35,
   "cues": [
    "case:A"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "c01-cases-02",
   "scene": "c01-cases",
   "lang": "en",
   "text": "Case B is naṣb, with fatha. This is the new one we add today.",
   "pause": 0.35,
   "cues": [
    "case:B"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "c01-cases-03",
   "scene": "c01-cases",
   "lang": "en",
   "text": "Case C is jarr, with kasra. We have learned this one too.",
   "pause": 0.35,
   "cues": [
    "case:C"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "c01-cases-04",
   "scene": "c01-cases",
   "lang": "en",
   "text": "Case D is called",
   "pause": 0.4,
   "cues": [
    "case:D"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "c01-cases-05",
   "scene": "c01-cases",
   "lang": "ar",
   "text": "جَزْم",
   "pause": 0.4,
   "cues": []
  },
  {
   "id": "c01-cases-06",
   "scene": "c01-cases",
   "lang": "en",
   "text": "Its sign is sukūn. It is for verbs. It comes later.",
   "pause": 0.6,
   "cues": []
  },
  {
   "id": "c01-scope-01",
   "scene": "c01-scope",
   "lang": "en",
   "text": "Only past verbs. For example, he wrote.",
   "pause": 0.4,
   "cues": [
    "scope:1"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "c01-scope-02",
   "scene": "c01-scope",
   "lang": "ar",
   "text": "كَتَبَ",
   "pause": 0.4,
   "cues": []
  },
  {
   "id": "c01-scope-03",
   "scene": "c01-scope",
   "lang": "en",
   "text": "And order verbs. For example, write!",
   "pause": 0.4,
   "cues": []
  },
  {
   "id": "c01-scope-04",
   "scene": "c01-scope",
   "lang": "ar",
   "text": "اُكْتُبْ",
   "pause": 0.4,
   "cues": []
  },
  {
   "id": "c01-scope-05",
   "scene": "c01-scope",
   "lang": "en",
   "text": "Present verbs come later.",
   "pause": 0.4,
   "cues": []
  },
  {
   "id": "c01-scope-06",
   "scene": "c01-scope",
   "lang": "en",
   "text": "And only one sign of naṣb: the fatha, alone or with tanween.",
   "pause": 0.35,
   "cues": [
    "scope:2"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "c01-scope-07",
   "scene": "c01-scope",
   "lang": "en",
   "text": "The other signs, for the dual and some plurals, come later in the course. Each group gets its own lesson.",
   "pause": 0.6,
   "cues": []
  }
 ]
}